# Frontend Agent Rules

## Hard rules
* **Thin routes, fat forms:** Route files own routing only (`beforeLoad`, layout shell, title). Put fetch/mutate/form state and CRUD UI in `frontend/src/components/forms/`.
* **shadcn first:** Prefer components from `#/components/ui` (shadcn/ui, New York, lucide). Do not add new UI libraries. Do not hand-roll Button/Input/Dialog/Select/Table/Tabs/Checkbox/Badge/Dropdown when a shadcn primitive exists or can be added via the shadcn CLI into `components/ui/`.
* **Reuse tokens:** Use existing CSS variables (`--ink`, `--muted`, `--line`, `--surface`, …), `cn()` from `#/lib/utils`, and `#/lib/ui-classes` helpers when a shadcn component is not the right fit yet. Do not invent parallel design systems.
* **Minimal changes:** Smallest diff. Match existing page rhythm. No drive-by restyles of unrelated pages.
* **Type-safe:** No `any`. Keep TanStack Router types happy; run `npm run generate-routes` after adding/renaming route files.

## Where files go

```
frontend/src/
  routes/                      # TanStack file routes — thin
    admin/route.tsx            # layout, sidebar, authz gate
    admin/<page>.tsx           # title + render a form component
  components/
    ui/                        # shadcn primitives ONLY (cli-generated)
    forms/                     # feature CRUD + interactive forms
      auth/                    # LoginForm, RegisterForm, …
      admin/                   # AppConfigForm, UsersAdminForm, UserDetailForm, …
      shared/                  # PasswordInput and other form-only shared bits
    Header.tsx / Footer.tsx    # app chrome
    home/                      # marketing sections
  context/                     # AuthProvider, BrandingProvider
  lib/                         # apiFetch, ui-classes, useDebouncedValue, types
```

**Imports:** use `#/…` (see `package.json` imports map).

### Forms / CRUD placement

* Put **all** create / read / update / delete UI and its hooks, local state, debounced search, toasts, confirm dialogs, and API calls under `components/forms/`.
* Folder by domain when a feature grows (`forms/admin/`, `forms/auth/`). Flat files are fine for small forms.
* A route should look like: gate in `beforeLoad` → short page header → `<SomeForm />`.
* Do **not** put large interactive trees (tables with row actions, editors, multi-step saves) inline in `routes/`.
* Shared non-form chrome (admin sidebar, breadcrumbs) stays in the route layout or `components/` outside `forms/`.
* When touching existing misplaced CRUD (e.g. a large editor outside `forms/`), move it into `forms/<domain>/` as part of that change if the diff stays focused.

### shadcn usage

* Config: `frontend/components.json` (aliases → `#/components/ui`, icons → lucide).
* Add missing primitives with the shadcn CLI into `src/components/ui/` — do not copy-paste one-off styled clones.
* Compose feature UI from shadcn primitives inside `forms/`; do not fork primitives into `forms/`.
* Prefer: Button, Input, Label, Textarea, Checkbox, Select, Dialog, DropdownMenu, Table, Tabs, Badge, Skeleton, Tooltip, Separator, Collapsible, Sheet (mobile admin nav if needed).
* Toasts: keep `react-hot-toast` (already wired in `__root.tsx`) unless the project standardizes on a shadcn toaster later.
* Icons: `lucide-react` only.

## Route conventions (TanStack Router)

* File routes under `src/routes/`; regenerate with `npm run generate-routes`.
* Auth: `bootstrapAuth()` in `beforeLoad`; redirect unauthenticated users.
* Admin authz: there are two roles, `user` and `admin` (from `/auth/validate`). Use `isAdmin` from `useAuth()` in components and `isAdminUser(user)` in `beforeLoad`. There is no permission system; feature access comes from the user's plan (`user.plan` from `useAuth()`).
* Admin layout (`/admin/route.tsx`): its `beforeLoad` guards every admin page; sidebar plus breadcrumb above content.
* After actions that change the **current** user’s role, call `refreshAuth()`.

## Data & API

* Use `apiFetch` / `apiUpload` from `#/lib/api`. Expect `ApiResponseDto<{ success, message, data }>`.
* Surface failures with concise toasts; show inline field errors when the API returns `data.fields`.
* Debounce search with `useDebouncedValue(..., 250)` unless a page already uses another agreed delay.
* Loading: skeletons or a small spinner. Empty: short message + one CTA. Error: message + Retry.
* Destructive actions: confirm via shadcn `Dialog` (or native `<dialog>` only if already present and untouched).

## UX standard (keep pages cohesive)

Clean, calm, hierarchical SaaS — one product, not a collage of page styles.

* **Hierarchy:** Clear page title → section headings → quiet helper/`sm`/`xs` text. Not everything is loud.
* **Copy:** Short labels and one-line hints. No large explanatory paragraphs when a sentence will do.
* **Cards sparingly:** Use containment only to group related controls or create an interaction surface. Prefer spacing/typography over nested boxes. No cards in heroes unless the design already requires it.
* **One primary action** per view; secondary actions quieter; destructive separated.
* **Forms:** Related fields grouped, labels on every input, helper text small, progressive disclosure for rare options.
* **Tables:** Scanable; important columns first; `overflow-x-auto` on small screens; optional card collapse on mobile.
* **A11y:** Visible focus, keyboard operable menus/dialogs, `aria-expanded` / `aria-checked="mixed"` where used, labels on inputs.
* Before restyling: reuse existing tokens/components. Fix the shared primitive, not one page’s one-off CSS.

## Auth context

* `useAuth()` exposes `user`, `isAuthenticated`, `isAdmin`, `login`, `logout`, `refreshAuth`, `isLoading`.
* Header “Admin” link is shown when `isAdmin` is true.

## Done criteria

* New CRUD lives under `components/forms/` (domain subfolder when useful)
* UI built from `#/components/ui` + existing tokens; no new UI library
* Route file stays thin (gate + shell + form component)
* `generate-routes` run if routes changed
* Loading / empty / error / success states present for interactive views
* Responsive enough for mobile admin use (sidebar icon-only pattern already used)
